From: JamesDSP root fork - 0007
Subject: [PATCH 0007] engine: capture tap (IN/OUT WAV lanes) for microphone-free
 verification

Every acceptance run of this module so far had to record the speaker with a
microphone (docs/ACCEPTANCE-COLOROS-v2.1.2.md).  That path is acoustic: the
microphone chain compresses the signal (~1.6:1 measured on this device) and
adds the room, so it can prove "something audible came out" but never "this
exact PCM reached the HAL".  The tap captures the samples the engine is about
to hand to AudioFlinger instead.

Two lanes are taken from the same render call, so a before/after pair is always
frame aligned:

  lane 0 (IN)  the effect input buffer  -> what AudioFlinger mixed for us
  lane 1 (OUT) the rendered engine output -> the bytes generic_process()
                                            returns to AudioFlinger, i.e. the
                                            same object the vendor AF35 dump
                                            records (bit-exact, see
                                            docs/SPEAKER-TAP-RESEARCH.md)

The render thread only does a bounds checked memcpy into a preallocated ring:
no allocation, no lock, no syscall, no log.  A dedicated writer thread drains
the ring into canonical WAV files (or leaves the data for jdsp_tap_read()); on
overrun the ring drops the oldest frames and counts them, it never blocks the
audio thread.

Default state is OFF: the effect module holds tap == NULL, so the two hook
calls in generic_process() are a NULL check each and nothing else happens - no
allocation, no memcpy, no file, no log.  A capture is armed explicitly through
the effect parameter channel (32001 with a jdsp_tap_config_t, 32002 reads a
jdsp_tap_status_t), which is handled before the write-lock gate so it needs no
engine key, is never queued into the deferred parameter path and never
persisted into the state file.

Interface: see jdsp_tap.h.  Device measurements, the -20 dB/1 kHz notch proof
and the bit-exactness check against the shipped vendor library are in
docs/SPEAKER-TAP-RESEARCH.md; the repo level usage is in
docs/ENGINE-TAP-AND-MIX-CHECK.md.

Host tests: native/test/test_tap.c (bit exact capture/read back for all five
formats, overrun policy, limit_frames, WAV header, concurrent producer and
consumer, NULL/unknown-format no-ops).
---
